Adapted files:

- src/halflife/integrity/prereg.py, from tools/prereg.py: the verify report
  with one problem per line, frozen content that never changes, ordering that
  cannot be rearranged, and a check that cannot be completed counted as a
  failure. The hash chain and beacon anchors are replaced by checks over git
  history.
- src/halflife/integrity/claimcheck.py, from tools/claimcheck.py: blanking
  addresses rather than claims (URLs, digests, list markers) without moving
  line numbers, an allowlist in which every entry needs a reason, and checking
  outbound drafts by default. Numbers must be claim markers backed by a named
  artifact instead of any banked value that rounds to them.
- src/halflife/integrity/freshness.py, from tools/freshness.py: a stale
  number (real but no longer current) fails, a selector that does not resolve
  is a failure rather than a skip, and the selector grammar stays small.
  Numbers are re-derived through committed derivations instead of document
  regular expressions.
- tests/test_gate_mutations.py, from tests/mutation_test.py: mutation tests
  that prove each gate can fail, with surviving mutations reported as holes.
- tests/test_integrity_prereg.py, tests/test_integrity_claimcheck.py, and
  tests/test_integrity_freshness.py: some cases follow the prereg, claimcheck,
  and freshness cases of tests/mutation_test.py.
